          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Off target by %lld arc-seconds": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld Bogensekunde neben dem Ziel"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "%lld Bogensekunden neben dem Ziel"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "variations": {
            "plural": {
              "one": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "Fuera del objetivo por %lld segundo de arco"
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "Fuera del objetivo por %lld segundos de arco"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Off target for about %@ s, at most %@° behind.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Etwa %1$@ s neben dem Ziel, höchstens %2$@° zurück."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "Off target for about %1$@ s, at most %2$@° behind."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fuera del objetivo durante unos %1$@ s, con un retraso máximo de %2$@°."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Off: set the exposure yourself. Long exposures and high gain bring up faint satellites; short ones keep the ISS or the Moon from burning out.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Aus: Belichtung selbst einstellen. Lange Belichtungen und hohe Verstärkung zeigen lichtschwache Satelliten; kurze verhindern, dass ISS oder Mond ausbrennen."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Desactivado: ajustar la exposición manualmente. Las exposiciones largas y la ganancia alta revelan satélites débiles; las cortas evitan que la ISS o la Luna se saturen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Offset": {
      "comment": "Position offset of the tracking aim",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Offset"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Desplazamiento"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "On target the whole pass.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Den ganzen Überflug auf dem Ziel."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "En el objetivo durante todo el paso."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "On target within": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Auf dem Ziel innerhalb"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "En el objetivo en"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Only point a telescope or camera at the Sun with a proper full-aperture solar filter fitted.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Teleskop oder Kamera nur mit montiertem Vollapertur-Sonnenfilter auf die Sonne richten."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Apuntar un telescopio o una cámara al Sol solo con un filtro solar adecuado de apertura completa colocado."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Only with a proper full-aperture solar filter on the scope and finder.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Nur mit geeignetem Vollapertur-Sonnenfilter an Teleskop und Sucher."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Solo con un filtro solar adecuado de apertura completa en el telescopio y el buscador."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Open in Maps": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In Karten öffnen"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Abrir en Mapas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Or enter it in Settings.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Oder in den Einstellungen eingeben."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "O introducirla en Ajustes."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Or enter where it points": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Oder eingeben, wohin es zeigt"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "O introducir hacia dónde apunta"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Orbital elements and the satellite catalogue (launch, orbit, radar cross-section) come from CelesTrak. Physical dimensions come from Jonathan McDowell's General Catalog of Artificial Space Objects (planet4589.org/space/gcat), under CC BY 4.0. Radio transmitters come from the SatNOGS DB (db.satnogs.org), under CC BY-SA 4.0. Deep sky objects come from OpenNGC by Mattia Verga, under CC BY-SA 4.0, star names from the IAU Working Group on Star Names, and comet orbits from the IAU Minor Planet Center.": {
      "comment": "Keep the names of people, organisations, catalogues, websites and licences as they are: CelesTrak, General Catalog of Artificial Space Objects, SatNOGS DB, OpenNGC, IAU, CC BY 4.0, CC BY-SA 4.0.",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bahnelemente und der Satellitenkatalog (Start, Bahn, Radarquerschnitt) stammen von CelesTrak. Physische Abmessungen stammen aus Jonathan McDowells General Catalog of Artificial Space Objects (planet4589.org/space/gcat) unter CC BY 4.0. Funksender stammen aus der SatNOGS DB (db.satnogs.org) unter CC BY-SA 4.0. Deep-Sky-Objekte stammen aus OpenNGC von Mattia Verga unter CC BY-SA 4.0, Sternnamen von der IAU Working Group on Star Names und Kometenbahnen vom IAU Minor Planet Center."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Los elementos orbitales y el catálogo de satélites (lanzamiento, órbita, sección eficaz de radar) proceden de CelesTrak. Las dimensiones físicas proceden del General Catalog of Artificial Space Objects de Jonathan McDowell (planet4589.org/space/gcat), bajo CC BY 4.0. Los transmisores de radio proceden de la SatNOGS DB (db.satnogs.org), bajo CC BY-SA 4.0. Los objetos de cielo profundo proceden de OpenNGC de Mattia Verga, bajo CC BY-SA 4.0; los nombres de estrellas, del IAU Working Group on Star Names, y las órbitas de cometas, del IAU Minor Planet Center."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Orbital inclination, degrees": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bahnneigung, Grad"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Inclinación orbital, grados"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Orbital period, minutes": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Umlaufzeit, Minuten"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Periodo orbital, minutos"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Out of shadow": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Aus dem Schatten"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fuera de la sombra"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Out of sight, carrying on along its path…": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Außer Sicht, folgt weiter seiner Bahn…"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fuera de la vista, continuando por su trayectoria…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Over the top": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Über den Zenit"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Por el cenit"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Over the top tilts the tube past the zenith; check it clears the mount and tripod first. Speeds are assumptions until measured on your HAZ46. \"On target\" is about half your field of view.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "„Über den Zenit“ kippt den Tubus über den Zenit hinaus; vorher prüfen, ob er an Montierung und Stativ vorbeikommt. Geschwindigkeiten sind Annahmen, bis sie an der eigenen HAZ46 gemessen sind. „Auf dem Ziel“ entspricht etwa dem halben Gesichtsfeld."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pasar por el cenit inclina el tubo más allá del cenit; comprobar antes que no choca con la montura ni el trípode. Las velocidades son estimaciones hasta medirlas en su HAZ46. «En el objetivo» es aproximadamente la mitad de su campo de visión."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Overpass": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Overpass"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Overpass"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Overpass needs your location to work out what's in your sky.": {
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Overpass benötigt den Standort, um zu berechnen, was am Himmel zu sehen ist."
